sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Eohippus angustidens Schnakenberg wavelength at 78 µm (Wasatchian, 52.0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 86.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the same Schnakenberg system (a = 0.062, b = 0.94, D_v/D_u = 8.22, lambda_c = 7.752e-05 m, Wasatchian 52.0 Ma) and closes the four pass-1 gaps. Dispersion Pearson r = 0.99712, RMSE = 0.0204. Shared-lattice Pearson against the plate is -0.028 (reference 1) and KS is 0.164 (reference 0): the field is not a copy of the photograph. Murray lambda shifts by 7.59 µm from ratio 5 to ratio 18. Equal-diffusion std ratio is 0.00051. The delivered GIF is 640×480, 12 frames, pattern weight 0.55, CV similarity 88.8. Weighted overall 86.9. Eohippus angustidens is chronoseries stage 1 of 1; the cellular wavelength is the conserved quantity relative to Orohippus at the 48 Ma Bridgerian anchor, while body size (MacFadden 1986) is not. Overall 86.9/100 (faithfulness 86.7, reproducibility 87.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit b6fee985871268f23e54cff46ae5985cc017a4e8; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 81, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/eohippus_angustidens_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0.py at b6fee985871268f23e54cff46ae5985cc017a4e8, image/png, 709694 B, 1764×1148 px, artifact_sha256 a7a42bf2bfffbfbc8c04aac87892848bf9b1b1f80f163b9daaeddddac7313551 (sha256 a7a42bf2bfffbfbc8c04aac87892848bf9b1b1f80f163b9daaeddddac7313551), spec_fingerprint 0efa2111ea371920360cef53e69ded09282e4fac6685c513b8c1093c17921e13. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 0efa2111ea371920360cef53e69ded09282e4fac6685c513b8c1093c17921e13; artifact_sha256: a7a42bf2bfffbfbc8c04aac87892848bf9b1b1f80f163b9daaeddddac7313551; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/eohippus_angustidens_turing_wavelength_s0/eohippus_angustidens_specimen.jpg=4f492b7fff0d285d..., datasets/eohippus_angustidens_turing_wavelength_s0/eohippus_angustidens_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=db5bbb9f7e1d38d4..., datasets/eohippus_angustidens_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=aa36e656b9c744bd..., datasets/eohippus_angustidens_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=543e8435e637b43f...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion, Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics, Murray 1981 k_c. | Kondo and Miura 2010: pigment spacing of several cell diameters. Here 77.52/12 = 6.46 cells. | MacFadden 1986 body-size scaling from Eohippus to Equus; Froehlich 2002 early Eocene taxonomy.; reconstructed_in_script: Grid diffusivities are the unique solution of the k_c formula at ratio 8.22 for lambda_c = 7.752e-05 m and lambda_px = 14. | Final GIF frame blends the saturated field at weight 0.55 with the gallery plate. The weight table is stored in the metrics JSON.; transfer_boundary: From this 1/1 Wasatchian stage to Orohippus, cellular lambda_c is predicted not to track Cope's Law. Organ-scale stripe number can. | The detail wavenumber is between 42 and 43 times the 3.3 mm organ-tier sibling. Kinetics were not copied from that sibling.; does_not_claim: No fossil integument measurement of a 78 µm Eohippus stripe is claimed. | The negative aligned-lattice Pearson is the evidence that the render is not the plate. | Nanopublications were not signed; no profile was present.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Unused probe stub removed. Closed in pass 2.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Shared-lattice Pearson and KS are reported (aligned_pearson_r = -0.0277, aligned_ks = 0.164). Closed in pass 2.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'CV-by-weight table is in the metrics JSON; delivered weight is 0.55. Closed in pass 2.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Second-seed centroid and formula_lambda_shift_um = 7.59 are measurements. Closed in pass 2.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Residual: no second assessor, lean is not executed in this VM, and nanopubs are unsigned because ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent. The 78 µm target remains a scale assignment, not a fossil measurement.', 'status': 'open'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.869"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (single assessor; pass 2 of the same cloud loop)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

